<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 40 — API Security Hardening.
    ratelimit/   fixed window, sliding window and GCRA (token bucket) limiters; GCRA in Redis shared by every
                 instance (resources/ratelimit/gcra.lua); per-client and per-tenant layers; RateLimit headers
    validation/  free text that is text (normalised, no controls or bidi overrides, length in code points) and an
                 email check that runs in linear time
    cors/        an exact-origin CORS allow-list
    csrf/        a Fetch Metadata resource isolation policy for cookie-authenticated endpoints
    tenancy/     tenant ids from the token, transactions scoped to a tenant for PostgreSQL row-level security
    web/         order-service's edge: /api (bearer tokens, CORS, rate limits) and /bff (session cookie, Fetch
                 Metadata, CSRF token), Bean Validation on a request DTO that cannot carry price or tenant
  resources/waf holds the OWASP CRS settings and rule exclusions for the JSON API, resources/tenancy the RLS schema,
  resources/gateway the Spring Cloud Gateway equivalent of the limits. verify/run.sh measures the limiters (and
  the Redis one against a real Redis), regular-expression backtracking, CORS matchers, CSRF and CORS in a real
  browser (Chromium), the CRS at four paranoia levels (Coraza), and tenant isolation in PostgreSQL 16.
-->
